From d9f16520621f261b611317ee0917cbf2ea9ce03c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:29:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: fuse SiLU into the convolution epilogue at schedule
 time

YOLO-style networks follow almost every convolution with SiLU (x*sigmoid(x)).
MNN's Convolution2DCommon only carries relu/relu6, so the Vulkan image backend
ran each SiLU as a separate VulkanUnary dispatch: for YOLOv9-t 320 that is 179
of the ~780 dispatches per inference, each a dependent launch that the GPU has
to drain before (~3.5 us on Apple AGX under Honeykrisp) plus a ~6 us kernel.

This adds a runtime fusion, so it applies to any already-converted model:

* schema: Convolution2DCommon.fusedActivation (int, default 0, appended at the
  end of the table so existing models and readers are unaffected). Non-zero
  values are UnaryOpOperation ids applied after bias/relu/relu6. Converters do
  not write it.
* core: Backend::onSupportFusedActivation() (default false) and a pass at the
  end of Pipeline::encode() that, for every UnaryOp whose input is produced by
  a Convolution/ConvolutionDepthwise command with a single consumer and no
  relu/relu6, asks the main backend; on yes it re-packs the convolution op with
  fusedActivation set, points it at the unary's output and drops the unary
  command. Fused op buffers are cached per original op so the execution cache
  survives resizes. Session outputs, quantized tensors, raster regions and
  shape-changing unaries are excluded.
* Vulkan image backend: accepts SILU for group-1 Convolution and
  ConvolutionDepthwise (same image-size check as onCreate). All conv epilogues
  gain a SILU variant selected through getPostTreatMacro: convolution1x1
  (3 kernels), convolutionDepthwise (2), col2Im (im2col path) and
  winogradTransformDest2_3_1. SiLU is evaluated in fp32 with the same
  expression as unaryImage.comp, also in the FP16 kernel variants. The new
  SPIR-V is appended to AllShader.cpp/.h and VulkanShaderMap.cpp (existing
  blobs untouched); macro.json lists the variants for makeshader.py.
* CPU backend: if a convolution op with fusedActivation reaches the CPU
  (fallback when the GPU declines the op), CPUBackend::onCreate wraps the
  execution and applies the unary function in place after the convolution
  (fp32 and fp16 cores), so correctness never depends on which backend ends
  up running the op.

Measured on Apple M1 (Fedora Asahi, Mesa 26.1.8 Honeykrisp), YOLOv9-t 320,
batch 1, image backend, MNN_GPU_RECORD_BATCH, next to a live NVR:

                       dispatches/inference   fp16 median   fp32 median
  before (batch mode)         783              12.1 ms       14.7 ms
  after                       604 (-179)       11.15 ms      14.0 ms

fp32 output is bit-identical to the unfused build (md5 301ed9a3). fp16 differs
slightly because SiLU now sees the fp32 accumulator instead of the fp16-rounded
tensor: max abs diff 2.0 vs the unfused fp16 output, and it is closer to the
fp32 reference (mean abs diff vs onnxruntime 0.0546 vs 0.0562). On 45 real
detector frames the post-processed detections are identical (36/36, max score
delta 0.003, max box-corner delta 0.37 px). Scheduled ops 469 -> 290.

